r  emir fritz  are the angels playing disguise with  devil's faces since the titan faces  are sort of like devil's faces emir  fritz was also called a goddess and  aaron is acting like the devil  to bring about a paradise for others to  protect the people he cares about but  for me this more so refers to the  aldians and people from parodies  like armin reiner annie and mikasa who  are trying to stop aaron from destroying  the world marlene's in the rest of the  world view aldians as devils and thus  they have devil's faces  and yet there are angels in their  actions working to save the people that  want them dead  mikasa even appeared to have wings at  one point when the flying titan appeared  behind her in the manga  probably the closest we get to an  angelic image  visually we see an aircraft sharing the  sky with a bird  again emphasizing the growing importance  of the skies  and how they're no longer human free and  safe we see statues explode including  statues of survey corps members with  their vertical maneuvering gear on  suggesting we're going to have heavy  losses on all sides  another lyric reads and i quote children  cling to their coins squeezing out their  wisdom end quote  and it's hard to even hear all the  lyrics in this song  i definitely didn't know what was going  on until i looked them up and that  further reflects the chaos and competing  voices in this season the lyric about  the children  clearly makes me think about aaron and  his colossal titans trampling them  children are victims of this war  too and keep in mind reiner annie  bertolt and marcel were kids when they  invaded parodies island initially  then gabby and falco as children entered  wars too  although wisdom has been squeezed out  aka nothing makes sense anymore  it reminds me of what harper lee said  about the war novel catch-22  she said it is the only war novel she's  ever read that makes any sense  the funny thing is catch 22 doesn't make  any sense  nothing that happens in it is rational  lee said that because  if a war novel does make sense it  actually doesn't make sense because  war doesn't make sense similarly attack  on titan portrays the often senseless  aspects of war the wise thing to do  would have been for aldian's marlenes  and the whole world to treat each other  with respect  the way they'd want to be treated that's  the golden rule from like every religion  and culture  treat others the way you want to be  treated if you don't want to get  subjugated by others don't subjugate  them  if you don't want to be treated unfairly  don't treat others unfairly if you don't  want others creating weapons of mass  destruction  don't create weapons of mass destruction  if everyone followed the golden rule  a lasting paradise could be possible  of course this rule is much easier said  than followed  and as in real life human fear hatred  thirst for revenge clouds people's  judgments and so the only way aaron can  see  to solve the problem now is to do  something as crazy as flattening the  world with colossal titans  we keep seeing explosion after explosion  foreshadowing the utter destruction  we're going to see this season it is  practically the end of the world or the  apocalypse that takes place  we continuously see signs of humanity  like towers and buildings being blown  away  suggesting that what remains of humanity  will have to start from scratch  the following lyrics destruction and  regeneration  point to that too aaron hopes that  through this destruction  through this hell a new paradise can  emerge there's a winston churchill quote  that goes like this  if you're moving through hell keep going  that quote seems to embody aaron the  attack titan  and the idea of moving forward no matter  how bad it gets  another lyric goes you are the real  enemy  another quote that means something  completely different depending on who's  saying it for aaron the people that want  to wipe his people out are the enemy for  the world aaron is the enemy the devil  who's come to destroy them the question  is who  is the real enemy and many people have  even said that aaron our protagonist  has become the villain or enemy an  attack on titan and we're forced to ask  who is the real enemy marlei  aaron or you aka us meaning humanity  we've seen throughout history that  ordinary humans have been capable of  truly evil things and it makes me wonder  if this you are the real  enemy line can be said from the  perspective of the spine-like creature  that gave a mere titan powers in the  first place  this is an out-there theory but what if  this centipede-like creature represented  the natural world  and its goal was to wipe out humanity or  at least significantly lower the  population  because people continued to wage war  destroy and pollute  to the detriment of plants and animals  as we saw when the birds were falling  from the sky  earlier during this opening it did cross  my mind that the devil of the earth  which  could be the spine-like creature was  actually a manifestation of the earth's  will  that's finally turned against humans the  fact that mindless titans clearly get  energy from the sun  like plants and can manifest animal  qualities like the beast titan  does make you think but anyways we jump  to lyrics of war  my war and then the word monster is  repeated  these words are sung while we see rain  falling on piles and piles of bodies  clearly this seems like the people aaron  trampled using the rumbling it's a nod  to his eventual actions  and it's crazy to think that our  protagonists would be capable of doing  something so horrific  and of course then it zooms into the  attack titan statue with other titans  attached to it seemingly following him  or  trying to catch him and the words  monster are repeated  suggesting to the viewers that aaron is  the monster or at least he is from many  people's perspectives  and even from the world's perspective  the statue looks like the titan  continues 